## TypeScript Rules

### Strict Mode
- TypeScript strict mode is enabled - honor it
- Never use `any` - use proper types, generics, or `unknown`
- One explicit exception: `[key: string]: any` in `SceneObject.properties` for extensibility

### Type Patterns
- Use discriminated unions for type-safe branching
- Export types from the module where they're defined
- Use interfaces for objects, type aliases for unions/primitives
- JSDoc comments on all exported functions and complex types

### Examples

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Discriminated union for step types
type StepType = 'info-card' | 'move-item';
interface SimStep {
  type?: StepType | null;
  // ... type-specific fields
}

// ✅ Good: Generic with constraints
function findByProperty<T extends { id: string }>(items: T[], id: string): T | undefined {
  return items.find(item => item.id === id);
}

// ❌ Bad: Using any
function processData(data: any) { ... }
```

---

## React Patterns

### Component Structure
- Functional components only, no class components
- Components in `src/components/` with `.tsx` extension
- One component per file (exceptions: related sub-components)
- Use React.FC sparingly, prefer explicit prop types

### Hook Patterns
```typescript
// Memoize expensive computations
const parsedSelection = useMemo(() => parseSelectionId(selectedObjectId), [selectedObjectId]);

// Memoize callbacks that are passed as props
const handleClick = useCallback((id: string) => {
  setSelectedId(id);
}, []);

// Use refs for mutable values that don't trigger re-renders
const hasNotifiedRef = useRef(false);

// Use refs for stale closure prevention in event handlers
const dragStateRef = useRef<DragState | null>(null);
useEffect(() => {
  dragStateRef.current = dragState;
}, [dragState]);
```

### State Management
- Local state with useState for component-specific data
- Context for global state (PopupContext pattern)
- Custom hooks for complex logic (useModelUpload, useProjects, useUndoRedo)
- No Redux or Zustand

---

## Three.js / React Three Fiber Patterns

### Performance
- Pre-allocate THREE objects outside render loops
- Use refs to avoid re-creating objects
- Memoize position/rotation/scale arrays
- Dispose of materials, geometries, and render targets on cleanup

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Pre-allocated objects
const raycaster = useRef(new THREE.Raycaster());
const groundPlane = useRef(new THREE.Plane(new THREE.Vector3(0, 1, 0), 0));

// ✅ Good: Memoized transform arrays
const position = useMemo<[number, number, number]>(
  () => [obj.transform.x / 100, obj.transform.y / 100, -obj.transform.z / 100],
  [obj.transform.x, obj.transform.y, obj.transform.z]
);

// ✅ Good: Cleanup on unmount
useEffect(() => {
  return () => {
    renderTarget.dispose();
    material.dispose();
  };
}, [renderTarget, material]);
```

### Component Memoization
```typescript
// Use React.memo with custom comparator for 3D objects
const IndustrialPrimitive = memo(IndustrialPrimitiveInner, (prevProps, nextProps) => {
  return (
    prevProps.obj.id === nextProps.obj.id &&
    prevProps.obj.transform.x === nextProps.obj.transform.x &&
    // ... compare all relevant props
  );
});
```

---

## Error Handling Requirements

### Use PopupContext for User-Facing Errors
```typescript
import { usePopup } from '../contexts/PopupContext';

function MyComponent() {
  const { showPopup } = usePopup();
  
  const handleError = (error: Error) => {
    showPopup({
      type: 'error',
      title: 'Upload Failed',
      message: error.message
    });
  };
}
```

### Helper Functions
```typescript
import { createErrorPopup, createWarningPopup, createSuccessPopup } from '../contexts/PopupContext';

showPopup(createErrorPopup('Storage Full', 'Unable to save project. Please free up space.'));
```

### Error Handling Rules
- Never swallow errors silently - always log or display
- Use try/catch for async operations
- Provide actionable error messages for users
- Log technical details to console for debugging

---

## Testing Requirements

### Test Structure
- Tests co-located with source files: `Component.test.tsx`
- Describe blocks for logical grouping
- Test file structure: setup → tests by category

```typescript
describe('GlobalPopup', () => {
  describe('rendering', () => {
    it('does not render when no popup is shown', () => { ... });
    it('renders popup dialog when triggered', async () => { ... });
  });
  
  describe('accessibility', () => {
    it('has role="dialog"', async () => { ... });
  });
});
```

### Testing Patterns
- Use `renderWithProvider()` helpers for context-dependent components
- Use `waitFor` for async assertions
- Test user interactions with `@testing-library/user-event`
- Mock Three.js/WebGL in `src/test/setup.ts`

### Run Tests
```bash
npm run test          # Run once
npm run test:watch    # Watch mode
npm run test:coverage # Coverage report
```

