## Quality Checklist

Before completing any feature:
- [ ] TypeScript compiles with no errors (`npm run typecheck`)
- [ ] ESLint passes (`npm run lint`)
- [ ] Prettier formatted (`npm run format`)
- [ ] Tests pass (`npm run test`)
- [ ] Errors shown to users via PopupContext
- [ ] Edge cases handled (empty data, null values, loading states)
- [ ] Accessibility: ARIA labels, keyboard navigation, focus management
- [ ] Performance: No new memory leaks, dispose Three.js resources

---

## Common Gotchas

1. **Scene units vs world units**: Scene uses centimeters (transform.x), Three.js uses meters (divide by 100)
2. **Z-axis flip**: Scene Z is positive-forward, Three.js Z is negative-forward (`-obj.transform.z`)
3. **Stale closures**: Use refs for values accessed in event handlers
4. **IndexedDB limits**: Blob storage limited, warn users on large models
5. **Camera controls**: CameraControls from camera-controls lib, not drei's OrbitControls

